        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Body parts that come in pairs are usually said in the plural: *begiak* (eyes), *belarriak* (ears), *eskuak* (hands). If you mean just one, say which side: *esku eskuina* (right hand), *ezkerreko begia* (left eye)."
        },
        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Body parts in everyday expressions",
          "items": [
            "*Buruz ikasi* — learn by heart (literally: learn by head).",
            "*Bihotzez eskerrak* — heartfelt thanks.",
            "*Eskuak garbitu* — wash your hands; *esku bat eman* — lend a hand.",
            "*Hankaz gora* — upside down, a total mess (literally: legs up)."
          ]
        }
      ]
